  "note": "Private test IPA 759, for the maintainer's report of 16 November 2026 after the IPA 758 test (\"Les artefacts violet sont encore plus visibles et nombreux\", two screenshot frame captures and the log, then \"aide toi avec ce github : https://github.com/cheemu21/plumber-racer-2\"): the verified IPA 758 (run 43812588474, IPA 7f873529) with the S2Arm engine of patches 0001-0050 (run 43825107808, artifact 14207021472, verified pin acda5e89). Patch 0050: (1) Mario Kart World maps its terrain-cache arrays in pairs over the same physical pages (each pair's pools mapped by the same requests in 758's log), writes one set through the GPU (31565 / 31566 / 31567) and samples the other (31562 / 31563 / 31564); the tiled levels' tiles were already shared by physical memory, but each layer's mip tail was a tile of its own, uploaded from guest memory, which the GPU's writes never reach (level 5 of layer 0 of 31562 and 31564 magenta, all-zero ASTC blocks, in both captures). A tail of one 64 KB physical run is now shared too, keyed by the texture's shape, and the look line counts such tails; (2) 2,231 render-target upgrades in 758's 125 s log, all of textures taken from their storage (the game's dynamic-resolution targets, whose storage range changes with the size): such a texture with no packaged layout, in a colour format Apple GPUs render to, is made with render-target use (S2A_RB_CPU_RT=0 in env.txt turns it off). Patches 0001-0049 are those of 758. The RPCS3 Core, MeloNX, XeniaCore, the app and every other retained component are those of the base; the RetroAchievements session's later fork-gate commits are source only. Images that must change: S2ArmEngine and Runner. Build-only delivery: Flutter/native groups not-run. Nothing has run on an iPhone; no claim that the pink is gone or that the stutters are fewer until the maintainer's test.",
